cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Textreflow: Reading Order and Paragraph Reconstruction for Document Layout Detectors"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Choudhary
    given-names: Mudit
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-8880-0925"
repository-code: "https://github.com/mudit-choudhary/textreflow"
url: "https://github.com/mudit-choudhary/textreflow"
abstract: >-
  Turns the regions a layout detector finds (labelled boxes with their text
  lines) into ordered, typed blocks: column-aware reading order, paragraphs
  rebuilt across regions, columns and pages with document-level
  de-hyphenation, structure kept as block types, and page furniture removed
  from the flow. Run on Docling's own layout over 60 arXiv papers, it cuts the
  share of paragraphs beginning mid-sentence from 12.5% (Docling's document
  model) to 2.4%.
keywords:
  - document parsing
  - reading order
  - layout analysis
  - retrieval-augmented generation
license: Apache-2.0
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-21"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22872013"          # concept DOI: always resolves to the latest version
